fore it, for the agents panel. A row written before the count parsed `Item.payload` keeps its stored `questionsAsked` of 0, which the transcript row and the shelf still draw; the panel, the ledger and the analysis recount it. Ledger copies of runs deleted before that are never recounted, so the history's per-run question average leaves out every copy without its history figures. Writes of one run are serialized; after the row, `Run.runOutcomes` keeps the newest per pull request (keyed case-folded, `pullRequestOutcomeKey`) for the run's wire projection (`DisplayedPullRequest.outcome`), and the list is announced through `PullRequestCaptureService.announceOutcome`, chained on the capture pass's per-run order so neither writer re-sends a list the other has moved; a failure there is logged without refusing the call. Only a pull request on the run's displayed list carries its outcome to the renderer. The stats module copies each row into `usage_activity` (Stats).
